{% aside type="note" %}
Domain reselling in FOSSBilling is functional but has some limitations. We're working on improvements.
{% /aside %}

Use domain products when you want clients to search, register, renew, or transfer domains through a supported registrar integration.

## What Works

- Domain registration, renewal, and transfers
- WHOIS lookup for availability checks
- Support for popular registrars

## Current Limitations

| Limitation | Details |
|------------|---------|
| Static pricing | You set prices per TLD manually — FOSSBilling doesn't pull live pricing from registrars |
| Hard-coded TLDs | Available TLDs are defined in each registrar module |
| Limited registrars | Only specific registrars are supported (see below) |

## Supported Registrars

Find installable registrar extensions in the [Extension Directory](https://extensions.fossbilling.org/).

### Bundled Options

**System → Domain Registration** lists the adapters available in your installation.

- **[Namecheap](https://www.namecheap.com/)** connects to the Namecheap reseller API.
- **ResellerClub** requires you to authorize your FOSSBilling server's IP address under **Settings → API** in its reseller control panel.
- **Custom** lets you handle domain orders manually and check availability via WHOIS.
- **Email** sends domain orders through PHP's `mail()` function, bypassing FOSSBilling's configured mail transport. It can check availability via WHOIS.

### Manually Installed Options

- [Generic EPP](https://github.com/getnamingo/fossbilling-epp-registrar) supports registries that use EPP, including Hostmaster.ua.
- [FRED Registry](https://github.com/getpinga/fossbilling-epp-fred) is an adapter for FRED-based registries.

## Setting Up Domain Reselling

{% steps %}
1. Get API credentials from your chosen registrar
2. Go to **System → Domain Registration** in FOSSBilling
3. Configure the registrar settings
4. Set up pricing for each TLD you want to sell
5. Enable the TLDs you want to offer
{% /steps %}

Need a registrar that is not supported yet? See [Creating a Registrar Integration](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-registrar-integration/).
